> Module Section151
> Using Definitions as W
> Using Section152 as S152
> Using Section2 as S2
> Using Section68 as S68

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ExemptionAmount:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input period content W.TaxPeriod
  input adjusted_gross_income content money
  applicable scope S68.ApplicableAmount
  filing scope S2.FilingStatusFor
  output amount content money

declaration scope PersonalExemptions:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input period content W.TaxPeriod
  input adjusted_gross_income content money
  filing scope S2.FilingStatusFor
  dependents_scope scope S152.DependentsOf
  exemption scope ExemptionAmount
  output dependents content list of W.Entity
  output total content money
```

```catala
declaration ordinary_phaseout_thresholds content list of money
  equals [$0; $2500; $5000; $7500; $10000; $12500; $15000; $17500; $20000; $22500; $25000; $27500; $30000; $32500; $35000; $37500; $40000; $42500; $45000; $47500; $50000; $52500; $55000; $57500; $60000; $62500; $65000; $67500; $70000; $72500; $75000; $77500; $80000; $82500; $85000; $87500; $90000; $92500; $95000; $97500; $100000; $102500; $105000; $107500; $110000; $112500; $115000; $117500; $120000; $122500]

declaration separate_phaseout_thresholds content list of money
  equals [$0; $1250; $2500; $3750; $5000; $6250; $7500; $8750; $10000; $11250; $12500; $13750; $15000; $16250; $17500; $18750; $20000; $21250; $22500; $23750; $25000; $26250; $27500; $28750; $30000; $31250; $32500; $33750; $35000; $36250; $37500; $38750; $40000; $41250; $42500; $43750; $45000; $46250; $47500; $48750; $50000; $51250; $52500; $53750; $55000; $56250; $57500; $58750; $60000; $61250; $62500; $63750; $65000; $66250; $67500; $68750; $70000; $71250; $72500; $73750; $75000; $76250; $77500; $78750; $80000; $81250; $82500; $83750; $85000; $86250; $87500; $88750; $90000; $91250; $92500; $93750; $95000; $96250; $97500; $98750; $100000; $101250; $102500; $103750; $105000; $106250; $107500; $108750; $110000; $111250; $112500; $113750; $115000; $116250; $117500; $118750; $120000; $121250; $122500; $123750]
```

§151. Allowance of deductions for personal exemptions

(a) Allowance of deductions

In the case of an individual, the exemptions provided by this section shall be allowed as deductions in computing taxable income.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section151:b0003; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section151(a); source-lines: 3-5; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope PersonalExemptions:
  definition filing.world equals world
  definition filing.taxpayer equals taxpayer
  definition filing.period equals period
  definition dependents_scope.world equals world
  definition dependents_scope.taxpayer equals taxpayer
  definition dependents_scope.candidates equals W.dependency_candidates of world
  definition dependents_scope.period equals period
  definition exemption.world equals world
  definition exemption.taxpayer equals taxpayer
  definition exemption.period equals period
  definition exemption.adjusted_gross_income equals adjusted_gross_income
  definition dependents equals dependents_scope.dependents
```

(b) Taxpayer and spouse

An exemption of the exemption amount for the taxpayer; and an additional exemption of the exemption amount for the spouse of the taxpayer if a joint return is not made by the taxpayer and his spouse, and if the spouse, for the calendar year in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins, has no gross income and is not the dependent of another taxpayer.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section151:b0004; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section151(b); source-lines: 7-9; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope PersonalExemptions:
  definition total equals
    let candidates equals W.dependency_candidates of world in
    let qualifying_children equals
      list of child among candidates such that
        exists possible_taxpayer among candidates such that
          not (W.same_entity of child, possible_taxpayer)
          and S152.qualifying_child_holds of
                world, possible_taxpayer, child, period in
    let taxpayer_count equals 1 in
    let spouse_count equals
      match filing.spouse with pattern
      -- Absent: 0
      -- Present content spouse:
          if W.has_full_year_joint_return of world, taxpayer, spouse, period
          then 1
          else if filing.status = S2.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
             and (W.gross_income_individual of world, spouse, period) = $0
             and not (exists possible_taxpayer among candidates such that
               not (W.same_entity of possible_taxpayer, taxpayer)
               and not (W.same_entity of possible_taxpayer, spouse)
               and S152.qualifying_relative_relationship of
                     world, spouse, possible_taxpayer, period
               and not (qualifying_children contains spouse)
               and not (S152.were_spouses of
                          world, spouse, possible_taxpayer, period)
               and not (S152.filed_joint_return of world, spouse, period))
          then 1 else 0 in
    let dependent_count equals
      dependent_exemption_count of dependents in
    let spouse_dependent_count equals
      match filing.spouse with pattern
      -- Absent: 0
      -- Present content spouse:
          if W.has_full_year_joint_return of world, taxpayer, spouse, period
          then
            let spouse_dependents equals
              (output of S152.DependentsOf with {
                -- world: world -- taxpayer: spouse
                -- candidates: candidates -- period: period }).dependents in
            combine all spouse_dependent among spouse_dependents
            in count initially 0
            with if dependents contains spouse_dependent
                 then count else count + 1
          else 0 in
    (exemption.amount * (taxpayer_count + spouse_count))
    + (dependent_exemption_total of exemption.amount,
         (dependent_count + spouse_dependent_count))
```

(c) Additional exemption for dependents

An exemption of the exemption amount for each individual who is a dependent (as defined in section 152) of the taxpayer for the taxable year.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section151:b0005; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section151(c); source-lines: 11-13; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration dependent_exemption_count content integer
  depends on dependents content list of W.Entity
  equals combine all dependent among dependents
         in count initially 0 with count + 1

declaration dependent_exemption_total content money
  depends on exemption_amount content money,
             dependent_count content integer
  equals exemption_amount * dependent_count
```

(d) Exemption amount

For purposes of this section-


```catala
scope ExemptionAmount:
  definition applicable.world equals world
  definition applicable.taxpayer equals taxpayer
  definition applicable.period equals period
  definition filing.world equals world
  definition filing.taxpayer equals taxpayer
  definition filing.period equals period
```

    (1) In general

    Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term "exemption amount" means $2,000.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section151:b0007; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section151(d)(1); source-lines: 19-21; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope ExemptionAmount:
  definition amount equals
    if exemption_suspended of period then $0
    else if not (phaseout_applies of adjusted_gross_income, applicable.amount)
    then $2000
    else
      let reduction equals
        phaseout_reduction of adjusted_gross_income, applicable.amount,
                              filing.status in
      if reduction >= $2000 then $0 else $2000 - reduction
```

    (2) Exemption amount disallowed in case of certain dependents

    In the case of an individual with respect to whom a deduction under this section is allowable to another taxpayer for a taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which the individual's taxable year begins, the exemption amount applicable to such individual for such individual's taxable year shall be zero.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section151:b0008; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section151(d)(2); source-lines: 23-25; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration exemption_after_other_taxpayer_claim content money
  depends on ordinary_amount content money,
             deduction_allowable_to_another_taxpayer content boolean
  equals
    if deduction_allowable_to_another_taxpayer then $0 else ordinary_amount
```

    (3) Phaseout


```catala
declaration phaseout_applies content boolean
  depends on adjusted_gross_income content money,
             applicable_amount content money
  equals adjusted_gross_income > applicable_amount
```

        (A) In general

        In the case of any taxpayer whose adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b), the exemption amount shall be reduced by the applicable percentage.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section151:b0010; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section151(d)(3)(A); source-lines: 29-31; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration phaseout_excess content money
  depends on adjusted_gross_income content money,
             applicable_amount content money
  equals
    if phaseout_applies of adjusted_gross_income, applicable_amount
    then adjusted_gross_income - applicable_amount
    else $0
```

        (B) Applicable percentage

        For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term "applicable percentage" means 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b). In the case of a married individual filing a separate return, the preceding sentence shall be applied by substituting "$1,250" for "$2,500". In no event shall the applicable percentage exceed 100 percent.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section151:b0011; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section151(d)(3)(B); source-lines: 33-35; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration phaseout_reduction content money
  depends on adjusted_gross_income content money,
             applicable_amount content money,
             filing_status content S2.FilingStatus
  equals
    let excess equals
      phaseout_excess of adjusted_gross_income, applicable_amount in
    let thresholds equals
      if filing_status = S2.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
      then separate_phaseout_thresholds
      else ordinary_phaseout_thresholds in
    let bands equals
      combine all threshold among thresholds
      in count initially 0
      with if excess > threshold then count + 1 else count in
    let reduction equals (2% * $2000) * bands in
    if reduction >= $2000 then $2000 else reduction
```

    (5) Special rules for taxable years 2018 through 2025

    In the case of a taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017, and before January 1, 2026, the term "exemption amount" means zero.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section151:b0012; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section151(d)(5); source-lines: 37-39; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration exemption_suspended content boolean
  depends on period content W.TaxPeriod
  equals period.tax_year >= 2018 and period.tax_year <= 2025
```
